# Line endings are a property of the repository, not of each contributor's
# local `core.autocrlf`. Text files are stored and checked out as LF on every
# platform, so a Windows checkout and an ubuntu-latest CI checkout produce
# byte-identical working trees.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text vs. binary, so genuinely binary files
# added later are left untouched without needing to be listed here. No file in
# this repo currently requires an explicit `binary` marker.
* text=auto eol=lf
